<title>UK: All London rail stations reopen after bomb threats.</title>
<headline>All London rail stations reopen after bomb threats.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>All five of the London railway stations closed during Monday mornings bomb threats have been reopened, British transport police said.</p>
<p>Mainline stations at Charing Cross, Kings Cross, Paddington and St Pancras were evacuated from about 7.15 am (0615 GMT). Baker Street underground station was also shut after police received a number of coded warnings that bombs had been left there.</p>
<p>No bombs were found after a thorough search and all the rail stations were reopened by noon.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
